{
    "background_story": "In the kingdom of Everwood, Prince Archer was next in line to the throne. Born into a centuries-old monarchy, he was groomed from a young age to one day rule with wisdom and justice. Archer's parents, the king and queen, taught him the intricacies of statecraft and the importance of serving the people. As he grew older, Archer became increasingly involved in the governance of the kingdom, earning the respect of the nobles and the admiration of the common folk. When his parents passed away, Archer ascended to the throne, vowing to uphold the traditions of his family while also introducing reforms to ensure the prosperity and happiness of his subjects. Under his leadership, Everwood flourished, and Archer became known as a fair and beloved monarch, revered by his people for generations to come.",
